**Site Note – Station T-03, Survey Area T**

The interpreted VES model comprises four layers with resistivities increasing monotonically with depth: 177.8 Ω·m (0–13.27 m), 265.8 Ω·m (13.27–16.67 m), 1064.5 Ω·m (16.67–25.48 m), and 2584.7 Ω·m (basement, >25.48 m). Applying the curve-type convention: for layers 1-2-3, r1 < r2 < r3 → A; for layers 2-3-4, r2 < r3 < r4 → A. The derived curve type is therefore "AA" (writable as "A"), not the "HA" type listed in the file. An H-type segment requires a resistivity decrease between the first two layers, which is not observed here (177.8 → 265.8 is an increase). This indicates a mismatch between the stated classification and the actual layer resistivity values, warranting review before use by the drilling team.

{"curve_type_stated": "HA", "label_issue_flagged": true}

